{"name":"Concord Buff","hex":"#e2ceb0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"concord","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of agreement; harmony; union.","An agreement by stipulation; a compact; a covenant; a treaty or league."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A variety of sweet American grape, with large dark blue (almost black) grapes in compact clusters; a Concord grape."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/concord"},{"term":"buff","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Undyed leather from the skin of buffalo or similar animals.","A tool, often one covered with buff leather, used for polishing."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of the color of buff leather, a brownish yellow.","Unusually muscular."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/buff"}],"entries":[{"title":"Buff (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Buff is a light brownish yellow, ochreous colour, typical of buff leather. Buff is a mixture of yellow ochre and white: two parts of white lead and one part of yellow ochre produces a good buff, or white lead may be tinted with French ochre alone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Chamois-natural.jpg/330px-Chamois-natural.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buff_(colour)","wikidata":"Q2085487"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Standard_Buff.jpg/250px-Standard_Buff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/Standard_Buff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Standard_Buff.jpg/250px-Standard_Buff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buff after A. Maerz[9]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStanda